- (analyze) Analyze changed files for informed decision making
  - Run: git diff --cached --name-only
  - Show: List of staged files to help you choose appropriate commit type

- (select-type) Choose commit type based on your understanding of the changes
  - feat: A new feature (correlates with MINOR version bump)
    (feat)
  - fix: A bug fix (correlates with PATCH version bump)
    (fix)
  - docs: Documentation only changes
    (docs)
  - style: Code style changes (whitespace, formatting, missing semicolons, etc.)
    (style)
  - refactor: Code refactoring that doesn't fix bugs or add features
    (refactor)
  - perf: Performance improvements
    (perf)
  - test: Adding or correcting tests
    (test)
  - build: Changes affecting build system or external dependencies
    (build)
  - ci: Changes to CI configuration files and scripts
    (ci)
  - chore: Other changes that don't modify src or test files
    (chore)
  - revert: Reverting previous commits
    (revert)

- (breaking-change) Check for breaking changes
  - Ask: Does this commit introduce breaking API changes?
  - If yes: You can either add '!' after type/scope OR use BREAKING CHANGE footer
    (breaking)

- (scope) Provide scope if applicable
  - What is the scope of this change? (e.g., component, module, file)
  - Scope is optional - skip if unclear

- (description) Write concise description
  - Use imperative mood (e.g., "add" not "added" or "adds")
  - Start with lowercase letter
  - No period at the end
  - Keep under 72 characters

- (body) Add detailed explanation if needed
  - Body is optional but recommended for complex changes
  - Explain the motivation behind the change
  - Describe alternatives considered
  - Leave blank line before body content

- (footer) Add footers if applicable
  - BREAKING CHANGE: <description> (for breaking changes)
  - Closes #<issue-number> (to close issues)
  - Leave blank line before footer content

- (format) Review complete commit message format
  - @feat[1]: <type>(<scope>): <description>
  - @fix[1]: <type>(<scope>): <description>
  - @docs[1]: <type>(<scope>): <description>
  - @style[1]: <type>(<scope>): <description>
  - @refactor[1]: <type>(<scope>): <description>
  - @perf[1]: <type>(<scope>): <description>
  - @test[1]: <type>(<scope>): <description>
  - @build[1]: <type>(<scope>): <description>
  - @ci[1]: <type>(<scope>): <description>
  - @chore[1]: <type>(<scope>): <description>
  - @revert[1]: <type>(<scope>): <description>

- (validate) Final validation checklist
  - Ensure type selection reflects actual change intent (your judgment, not automated)
  - Verify description is under 72 characters
  - Check proper Conventional Commits structure:
    <type>(<scope>): <description>

    [body]

    [footer]
  - Confirm breaking changes are properly marked if applicable
